Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:34:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C13's follow-ups, patch 3 (cld-advisor, at main's word in
 M23, item 5): THE 115 OLDER VERDICT LINES THE GATE READS AS CLAIMS ARE
 CLASSIFIED ONCE, WITH THEIR CLAUSES AND THE PAGE'S WORDS, AND THE GATE HOLDS
 THEM BY NAME WITH THEIR CLASS

Main's M23, item 5: the gate selection-family reads every verdict line. The 115 older lines that it reads as claims are
classified once, each with a quotation: a deduction (the rule is not about it); a selection claimed by a finite
classification with a test of membership, or by a consistency condition that can fail (the family named); or a
selection claimed with neither, which gets a dated note on its arc and a register row if anything rests on it. The gate
then holds the older lines by name with their class. The classifying is reading; main checks every row it marks a
selection.

- frontier/B1905_.../verification/older_verdict_lines_classified.json (new): 115 rows, each the arc, its class, and its
  clauses, the gate's own reading of its verdict line, word for word. Four classes: 63 deduction; 27 no claim (the clause
  denies, conditions, mentions or reports a selection, or names one as a choice or an input: the gate's reading over-
  reads them, and the rule is not about them); 13 family named, each with the words on its page that name the
  classification or the condition (B218, B781, B860, B1104, B1141, B1199, B1265, B1294, B1409, B1476, B1477, B1869,
  B1879); 12 neither, on this reading (B44, B125, B266, B1154, B1228, B1230, B1235, B1258, B1298, B1406, B1806, B1857).
- scripts/gates/gates.py: older_selection_lines reads every verdict line before B1905 and the table: an older line read as
  a claim and not in the table, a row whose line no longer reads so or reads other clauses, a class not of the four, and
  a family named whose words are not on its page, are each reported, and the gate fails on any. Its message counts the
  classes. The reading of the lines from B1905 on is unchanged.
- tests/test_selection_family.py: one test: the table holds and its classes sum to 115; four plants, each reported (a
  row taken out, a class not of the four, a family's words not on the page, a row whose clauses differ); the twin, the
  table as it is, passes. One assertion of the test of the repository gains a dated line.

NOT DONE HERE, AND WHY: the dated notes on the twelve arcs of class neither, and register rows where something rests on
them. Main checks every row marked a selection first; the notes follow its check, so that a note is not written on a
row main reads otherwise.

BEFORE: the new test fails on the gate as it stood. The gate's tests, the gates' failing paths, B1905's lock, the ledger
of walls and the paper's manifest: 68 passed. Every gate passes but the count of landings.

0 of 19.
